--- (3) THE STATEMENT: derived vs environmental ---
  candidate A (thermodynamically derived): the phantom beats the dust's
    entropy at fixed m by 10.8-23.7 k_B/particle and IS the global max
    of S in the well (G084) -> TRUE for the boundary's CHARACTER.
  candidate B (environmental input): the entropy functional selects NO
    truncation; the cap 0.62 r_M is placed by g_ext (G119: ratio-form
    sqrt(a0/g_ext), kernel 6.13 kpc = MW 6.1 kpc) -> TRUE for the
    boundary's POSITION.
  HONEST RANKING: HYBRID -- thermodynamic in nature, environmental in
    placement; NOT fully derivable from the entropy comparison alone.
  Normalization trap: in G084's TG-proximity convention the comparison
    FLIPS (phantom 9.6 vs dust 36.4 k_B) -- mass-threshold-relative;
    the shared-reference convention at fixed m is the honest one.

